Title:
PEB Walking and Custom GetModuleHandle (GetModuleHandleReplacement)

Type:
Blog Post

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
This write-up explains how to implement a `GetModuleHandle` replacement by “walking” internal Windows loader structures instead of calling Win32 APIs that are commonly monitored or hooked by AV/EDR. It starts from the TEB (per-thread) to reach the PEB (per-process), then uses `PEB_LDR_DATA` and `LDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY` linked lists to enumerate loaded modules and retrieve a target DLL’s base address (`DllBase`). The post covers x86 vs x64 access patterns using segment registers (FS/GS) and offsets (e.g., GS:0x60 for the PEB pointer on x64). It highlights practical pitfalls like module order assumptions (and how .NET/CLR can shift list ordering) and discusses why this primitive is foundational for zero-import loaders. It’s primarily useful for malware developers, red team tool authors, and exploit/shellcode developers building stealthier runtime API resolution. It also touches on related internals like `BeingDebugged` and how list termination works in circular loader lists.

Technical Focus:
- TEB/PEB access via FS/GS segment registers and intrinsic reads (`__readgsqword`, `__readfsdword`)
- Windows loader data structures: `PEB_LDR_DATA`, `LDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY`, `LIST_ENTRY`
- Enumerating module lists (InLoadOrder/InMemoryOrder/InInitializationOrder) to obtain `DllBase`
- Case-insensitive Unicode string comparison for module name matching (`UNICODE_STRING`)
- Avoiding userland API hooks/IAT monitoring by direct structure traversal

Use Cases:
- Building a custom `GetModuleHandle` for stealthy loaders without Win32 API calls
- Bootstrapping position-independent shellcode (finding `ntdll.dll`/`kernel32.dll` base)
- Implementing custom `GetProcAddress` by combining module base discovery with export parsing
- Supporting reflective DLL loading stubs that must resolve APIs at runtime
- Assisting API unhooking workflows by locating `ntdll.dll` and comparing/patching `.text`

Keywords:
PEB walking, TEB, PEB, PEB_LDR_DATA, LDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY, LIST_ENTRY, UNICODE_STRING, __readgsqword, __readfsdword, GS segment, FS segment, ntdll.dll, kernel32.dll, kernelbase.dll, GetModuleHandle, GetProcAddress, IAT hooking, userland hooks, reflective DLL loading, shellcode API resolution